## 2. Installation, Deployment, and Lifecycle

### 2.1 Installation and Provisioning Methods

* **Sferical One & Gefion (NVIDIA DGX SuperPOD)**: Bare-metal OS images, firmware, and Shorewall firewall roles are provisioned via **NVIDIA Base Command Manager (BCM)** (`cmsh`) and **NVIDIA Mission Control** (`2.2.0`); Kubernetes AI workloads run on dedicated User Kubernetes Nodes via **NVIDIA Run:ai** ([NVIDIA Mission Control 2.2.0](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.nvidia.com%2Fmission-control%2Fdocs%2Fsystems-administration-guide%2F2.2.0%2Foverview.html), [NVIDIA BCM Third Party](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.nvidia.com%2Fbase-command-manager%2Fproduct-manuals%2Finstallation%2Fthirdparty)). Gefion P1 sandbox onboarding uses the `aicentre` CLI ([P1 CLI Docs](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fhpc.aicentre.dk%2Fcli%2F)).
* **Palantir AIP / Foundry**: Platform services are deployed and continuously upgraded via **Palantir Apollo** on Rubix across AWS, Azure, GCP, Oracle Cloud, or air-gapped on-premises clusters ([The Rubix Substrate](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fpalantir.com%2Fdocs%2Ffoundry%2Farchitecture-center%2Frubix%2F)). Client SDKs and CLIs install via:
  ```bash
  # Python Platform SDK (Apache-2.0, v1.112.0)
  pip install foundry-platform-sdk

  # Python Ontology SDK (OSDK)
  pip install <PACKAGE> --upgrade --extra-index-url "<INDEX-URL>"

  # TypeScript OSDK
  npm install @osdk/client @osdk/oauth
  npx @osdk/create-app

  # Foundry CLI (SuperRepo Beta - direct enrollment script)
  curl -sS "$FOUNDRY_URL/code/api/extension/install-script" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | bash

  # Compute Module OCI Build (linux/amd64 required)
  docker build . -t <image>:<tag> --platform linux/amd64
  ```
  ([foundry-platform-python](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fpalantir%2Ffoundry-platform-python), [Python OSDK](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fpalantir.com%2Fdocs%2Ffoundry%2Fontology-sdk%2Fpython-osdk%2F), [osdk-ts](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fpalantir%2Fosdk-ts), [Foundry CLI](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fpalantir.com%2Fdocs%2Ffoundry%2Fsuperrepo%2Ffoundry-cli%2F), [Compute Modules Containers](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fpalantir.com%2Fdocs%2Ffoundry%2Fcompute-modules%2Fcontainers%2F)).
* **Isambard-AI**: Client SSH certificate CLI `clifton` installs via WinGet or `mise use -g ubi:isambard-sc/clifton` ([BriCS Login](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.isambard.ac.uk%2Fuser-documentation%2Fguides%2Flogin%2F)). User software deploys via Lmod, Spack, Miniforge/`uv`, Apptainer (`apptainer build --fakeroot`), Podman-HPC (`podman-hpc`), and SquashFS archives ([BriCS Intro Tour](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.isambard.ac.uk%2Fuser-documentation%2Ftutorials%2Fintro-tour%2F)).
* **LUMI**: Software builds via EasyBuild (`module load EasyBuild-user` with `EBU_USER_PREFIX`), Spack (`spack-cpu`/`spack-gpu`), Singularity CE, `cotainr` (`cotainr build app.sif --system=lumi-g --conda-env=env.yml`), and unprivileged PRoot; direct Conda/pip installs on Lustre are discouraged ([LUMI EasyBuild](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.lumi-supercomputer.eu%2Fsoftware%2Finstalling%2Feasybuild%2F), [LUMI Singularity](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.lumi-supercomputer.eu%2Fsoftware%2Fcontainers%2Fsingularity%2F)).
* **JUPITER**: System software is versioned in EasyBuild stages (`Stages/2026`; older stages via `ml use $OTHERSTAGES`). Containers run via Apptainer built remotely via the JSC Container Build System (`sib` CLI) or `module load shpc`; Conda is disabled on HPC systems ([JUPITER Container Runtime](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fapps.fz-juelich.de%2Fjsc%2Fhps%2Fjupiter%2Fcontainer-runtime.html)).
* **El Capitan, Frontier, Aurora & BerzeLiUs**: Software stacks deploy via Lmod and Spack (`/sw/frontier` on Frontier, `/opt/aurora/<VERSION>/spack` RPATH on Aurora, `/software` on BerzeLiUs). Containers use rootless Podman initialized with `enable-podman` (El Capitan), Apptainer (Frontier, Aurora, BerzeLiUs — Docker is strictly prohibited on BerzeLiUs), `sbcast --send-libs` (Frontier), and Copper read-only cache (Aurora) ([LLNL Containers](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fhpc.llnl.gov%2Fdocumentation%2Fuser-guides%2Fusing-containers-lc-hpc-systems%2Fcontainers-gotchas), [NSC Apptainer](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nsc.liu.se%2Fsupport%2Fsystems%2Fberzelius-software%2Fberzelius-apptainer%2F), [ALCF Aurora PE](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.alcf.anl.gov%2Faurora%2Faurora-pe%2F)).

