### 4.3 Authentication, Authorization, and Cryptographic Signing (`07_security_auth_ports_limits.csv`)

* **Palantir AIP / Foundry**: OAuth 2.0 (`/multipass/api/oauth2/token`) supporting **Authorization Code + PKCE** (`S256`, `code_verifier` 43-128 chars, rotating `refresh_token` via `offline_access`) and **Client Credentials**, plus SAML 2.0 / OIDC SSO ([Writing OAuth2 Clients](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fpalantir.com%2Fdocs%2Ffoundry%2Fplatform-security-third-party%2Fwriting-oauth2-clients%2F)). Access control combines discretionary RBAC (`Owner`, `Editor`, `Viewer`) with Mandatory Access Controls: **Organizations** (disjunctive: membership in >=1 applied org), **Markings** (conjunctive: user must hold all applied markings), **CBAC**, and Restricted Views ([Organizations and Spaces](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fpalantir.com%2Fdocs%2Ffoundry%2Fsecurity%2Forgs-and-spaces%2F), [CBAC](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fpalantir.com%2Fdocs%2Ffoundry%2Fsecurity%2Fclassification-based-access-controls%2F)). Field-level encryption uses `CipherText`; Compute Module IPC verifies Rubix CA (`/etc/ssl/rubix-ca/ca.pem`) + `Module-Auth-Token`.
* **HPC Federated & Hardware MFA**:
  * **Isambard-AI**: Keycloak + GÉANT MyAccessID OIDC issues 12-hour Conch CA signed Ed25519 SSH certificates via `clifton` ([arXiv:2410.18411](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Farxiv.org%2Fhtml%2F2410.18411v1)).
  * **JUPITER**: Passphrase-protected Ed25519 SSH key + mandatory JuDoor `from=` IP/CIDR restriction + RFC 6238 6-digit TOTP MFA (skipped for FIDO/YubiKey or EuroHPC EFP certs) ([JUPITER Access](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fapps.fz-juelich.de%2Fjsc%2Fhps%2Fjupiter%2Faccess.html)).
  * **LUMI**: Passwordless SSH only (MyAccessID/MyCSC SSH public keys or EuroHPC EFP SSH certs); LUMI-O S3 keys via `auth.lumidata.eu` ([LUMI SSH Keys](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.lumi-supercomputer.eu%2Ffirststeps%2FSSH-keys%2F)).
  * **El Capitan / Frontier / Aurora**: SSHv2 with RSA SecurID hardware OTP (El Capitan CZ/RZ/SCF Zone PIN + OTP; Frontier 4-8 digit PIN + 6-digit tokencode) or SafeNet MobilePASS+ / CryptoCard 8-digit passcode (Aurora); internal cluster crypto uses ZeroMQ CURVE + MUNGE (Flux), MUNGE + HS256 JWT (Slurm), and DAOS mTLS certificates ([LLNL Access](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fhpc.llnl.gov%2Faccounts%2Faccessing-lc-systems), [OLCF Connecting](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.olcf.ornl.gov%2Fconnecting%2Findex.html), [ALCF Token](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.alcf.anl.gov%2Faccount-project-management%2Faccounts-and-access%2Fobtaining-a-token%2F)).
  * **BerzeLiUs & Gefion**: SUPR/NAISS + mandatory 6-digit TOTP 2FA (`nim.nsc.liu.se`) + verified SSH host key fingerprints on BerzeLiUs (Ampere ED25519 `SHA256:iZLFlrmwW7YbMXsR7TQxlrDfHUbQnFg5tSfB4GNCtGQ`; Hopper ED25519 `SHA256:uOAV28QYD1ZgZxx4KX+5oRUbUHBJLqxMSVTRJnW4RS4`); non-transferable DCAI credentials + SSH keys + public IP whitelisting for `xfer.dcai.dk` on Gefion ([NSC Getting Started](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nsc.liu.se%2Fsupport%2Fsystems%2Fberzelius-getting-started%2F), [P1 Gefion](https://hpc.aicentre.dk/providers/gefion/)).

### 4.4 Data Schemas, Serialization Formats, and Internal Grammars / DSLs

* **Foundry Resource Identifiers (RIDs)**: Strict grammar `ri.<service>.<instance>.<type>.<uuid>` (e.g., `ri.foundry.main.dataset.<uuid>`, `ri.ontology.main.ontology.<uuid>`, `ri.actions.main.action.<uuid>`); global services omit the instance token (`ri.aip-agents..agent.<uuid>`, `ri.language-model-service..language-model.gpt-5-2`) ([Create Dataset (v2)](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fpalantir.com%2Fdocs%2Ffoundry%2Fapi%2Fv2%2Fdatasets-v2-resources%2Fdatasets%2Fcreate-dataset%2F)).
* **Foundry Storage & JSON Wire Serialization**: Tabular datasets store **Apache Parquet** (`*.snappy.parquet`) and **Apache Iceberg**; in-memory/wire transfers use **Apache Arrow** / Arrow Flight SQL; REST v2 JSON serializes `Long` and `Decimal` as strings, `Date` as ISO 8601 local date (`YYYY-MM-DD`), `Timestamp` as ISO 8601 UTC (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`), and `Geoshape` as GeoJSON ([Apply Action (v2)](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fpalantir.com%2Fdocs%2Ffoundry%2Fapi%2Fv2%2Fontologies-v2-resources%2Factions%2Fapply-action%2F)).
* **HPC Resource & Storage Grammars**: Flux RFC 20 JSON resource graphs and TOML broker configs; DWS Kubernetes `v1alpha2` CRDs (`Storage`, `DirectiveBreakdown`, `Servers`) + `#DW jobdw` DSL; DAOS object class grammar (`EC_16P3GX`, `RP_4G1`, `rd_fac:3`, `cksum:crc32`); Lustre Progressive File Layout (PFL) striping grammar (`-E 256K -L mdt -E 8M -c 1 -S 1M -p performance ...`) ([Frontier Guide](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.olcf.ornl.gov%2Fsystems%2Ffrontier_user_guide.html), [ALCF DAOS](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.alcf.anl.gov%2Faurora%2Fdata-management%2Fdaos%2Fdaos-overview%2F)).